Overlay patch 0061: soh-torch CLI builds again (host tool only, NOT __IOS__).
Upstream 9.3.0 broke its own build-time extractor: #7301 ("Extractor: pass
Torch ROMs as big endian") changed SohTorch::Extract to take the ROM BYTES
(std::vector<uint8_t>, already big-endian) instead of a path, but
soh/assets/tools/torch-cli/main.cpp still passes the path string. soh-torch is
EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL, so upstream's default build never notices; ExtractAssets and
our scripts/extract-oot-o2r.sh both need it. Fix: read the file and normalize
.v64 (16-bit swapped) / .n64 (32-bit little-endian) dumps to .z64 order by the
first word, exactly what the game's Extractor does with
BitConverter::RomToBigEndian before calling Extract. The game itself does not
compile this file; the oracle and the iOS app are unaffected. Upstreamable as-is.
(D-079)

--- a/soh/assets/tools/torch-cli/main.cpp
+++ b/soh/assets/tools/torch-cli/main.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <filesystem>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <iterator>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -52,6 +54,30 @@
